// The played bed -- the mix the owner actually plants, 2026-09-09.
//
// Every headless figure in the lab's reports before this was taken on the
// harness default: eight herb founders of one species, and (until `ants_at`)
// a colony dropped on seedlings at frame 0. The owner does not play that
// box. They grow a mixed bed first and then add ants, and the difference is
// not cosmetic -- same binary, same seed, a colony founded at frame 0 holds
// 4-13 animals at 30,000 frames where one founded at 6,000 holds 31.
//
// **The mix is the owner's own, given 2026-09-09: grass, herb and shrub.**
// Each does a different job, which is the whole reason a mix is not just a
// denser lawn:
//
//   grass  -- the fast ground staple. No separate leaves, matures in 10, and
//             it keeps the bench lit: measured over 120,000 frames a grass
//             bed holds 0.562 of lamp light at the soil where herb falls to
//             0.240 and shrub to 0.110.
//   herb   -- the only shipped plant that sets fruit, matures in 60.
//   shrub  -- slow woody clumps, matures in 250. These are what make the bed
//             patchy rather than uniform, so distance to food is a real
//             quantity in it.
//
// **No tree, and that was measured rather than assumed.** A tree was in the
// first reading of the owner's answer, so it was rendered before anything
// was run on it: one tree founder becomes 79 plants and shades the bench to
// **0.008** of lamp light by frame 30,000 -- thirty times darker than the
// herb bed, with the low plants that actually feed a colony shaded out. A
// long run on a bed with a tree in it measures the canopy closing, not
// whatever else it was pointed at. Review card
// `20260909T232116894Z-2b3661` puts the choice to the owner; if the answer
// is "tree anyway", it is one more `Plant` line here and every figure taken
// on this file has to be retaken.
//
// **Twenty-two plants, laid out rather than spread.** `LabBox::founders`
// spaces one species evenly; a mix wants the shrubs apart from each other
// (they are the clumps) with grass and herb filling between, so the plants
// are placed by column here and `founders` is 0. Four shrubs at roughly
// 120-column spacing anchor the patches; six herbs and twelve grass fill in
// at 15-40 column gaps.
//
// **The colony arrives at frame 6,000, on the timeline.** That is the whole
// point of the file -- `Colony` in `timeline` rather than `placements` is
// what makes this the played bed instead of the harness one, and it is why
// `ants_at=` is ignored in scenario mode: the timeline decides.
(
    name: "played_bed",
    title: "THE PLAYED BED",
    question: "The mix the owner plants -- grass, herb and shrub grown for 6,000 frames, then a colony lands on it.",
    bed: (
        width: 512,
        height: 320,
        soil_depth: 96,
        ground_y: 160,
        compartments: 1,
        founders: 0,
        species: "grass",
        colonies: 0,
        colony_ants: 52,
        colony_species: "ant",
        predators: 0,
        lamp_spacing: 33,
        seed: 1,
        extra_walls: [],
    ),
    settings: [],
    placements: [
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 20),
        Plant(species: "herb",  x: 40),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 55),
        Plant(species: "shrub", x: 70),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 90),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 110),
        Plant(species: "herb",  x: 130),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 155),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 175),
        Plant(species: "shrub", x: 190),
        Plant(species: "herb",  x: 220),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 240),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 260),
        Plant(species: "herb",  x: 280),
        Plant(species: "shrub", x: 310),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 330),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 350),
        Plant(species: "herb",  x: 370),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 400),
        Plant(species: "shrub", x: 430),
        Plant(species: "herb",  x: 460),
        Plant(species: "grass", x: 490),
    ],
    timeline: [
        (at: 6000, every: 0, until: 0, what: Colony(species: "ant", x: 256, count: 52)),
    ],
    horizon: 120000,
)
